WEBVTT

00:01.750 --> 00:02.500
Um...

00:03.120 --> 00:05.670
Are you Senior Kushida?

00:07.500 --> 00:11.090
It's me! I'm your junior
from middle school!

00:11.090 --> 00:12.720
I'm Takuya Yagami!

00:12.720 --> 00:16.720
Yagami...
Oh, you're that Yagami?

00:16.720 --> 00:19.720
Yep!
Long time no see!

00:19.720 --> 00:21.350
You know him?

00:21.350 --> 00:24.810
Yeah.
We didn't interact much,

00:24.810 --> 00:27.730
but he's really smart,
so he left an impression on me.

00:28.360 --> 00:30.900
Do you know Yagami too?

00:30.900 --> 00:33.200
You went to the same
middle school as Kushida, right?

00:33.200 --> 00:35.990
No, I don't.

00:35.990 --> 00:39.700
I wasn't interested enough to learn about
people who didn't catch my attention.

00:39.700 --> 00:43.790
Does he know about Kushida's past too?

00:44.580 --> 00:47.580
I wouldn't be surprised if he does.

00:49.750 --> 00:52.590
I know this is sudden,
but I'd be glad if it's you.

00:52.590 --> 00:56.590
Would you be willing to partner with me
for the special exam?

00:56.590 --> 00:58.720
Are you sure you want
to partner with me?

00:58.720 --> 01:02.020
Wouldn't it be better to team up with
someone who's better at studying?

01:02.020 --> 01:03.180
Huh?!

01:03.180 --> 01:05.560
Since I don't know
my way around here yet,

01:05.560 --> 01:08.610
I'd like someone
I can trust as my partner!

01:08.610 --> 01:13.360
Um, could you give me a little
time to think about it?

01:13.360 --> 01:15.320
Of course!

01:15.320 --> 01:19.160
I'll hold off on partnering with anyone
else for now and wait for your answer.

01:28.170 --> 01:29.710
You're the outcast monster

01:29.710 --> 01:32.880
Hidin', hidin', ding-ding-ding

01:32.880 --> 01:34.760
Hidin', hidin'

01:36.340 --> 01:42.310
Hidin', hidin', ding-ding-ding

01:42.850 --> 01:46.180
Tell me what a genius is

01:46.180 --> 01:49.560
The one who creates singularities

01:49.560 --> 01:52.440
Don't you feed the monster

01:52.440 --> 01:58.490
The black outline has gotten bigger again

01:58.490 --> 02:02.580
Everyone is always the king's piece

02:02.580 --> 02:04.200
Hidin', hidin', ding-ding-ding

02:05.370 --> 02:09.120
How does it feel to see into the future?

02:09.120 --> 02:13.340
A monster made of lies

02:13.340 --> 02:17.380
The monster hidin, hidin',
go get him

02:17.380 --> 02:20.640
A twisted, unfair trigger

02:20.640 --> 02:24.060
Hidin', hidin', the maze thoughts

02:24.060 --> 02:27.140
Mysteries swimming in them

02:27.140 --> 02:30.190
Confused by truth and lies

02:30.190 --> 02:32.730
Are we the prey or the hunters?

02:33.480 --> 02:35.320
Hidin', hidin'

02:35.320 --> 02:36.740
Longing for the ordinary

02:36.740 --> 02:38.570
Hidin', hidin'

02:38.570 --> 02:40.360
Yes, you are the outcast monster

02:40.360 --> 02:46.950
Hidin', hidin', ding-ding-ding

02:54.540 --> 02:56.550
- This is awesome!
- They really have everything!

02:56.550 --> 02:57.630
Check this out.

02:57.630 --> 02:59.550
That's great!

03:00.050 --> 03:03.010
First-years really are carefree.

03:03.010 --> 03:06.140
Meanwhile, we're seriously
trying to find partners.

03:06.140 --> 03:09.310
Have you already forgotten
what you were like a year ago?

03:10.520 --> 03:12.980
I-I haven't forgotten, okay?

03:12.980 --> 03:14.940
I'm reflecting on it.

03:14.940 --> 03:20.200
So, we're looking for a first-year who
might agree to partner with Sudo, right?

03:20.200 --> 03:23.070
Let's start by talking to a group.

03:26.240 --> 03:27.700
Do you have a moment?

03:28.700 --> 03:33.000
We're looking for partners
for the upcoming special exam.

03:33.540 --> 03:36.210
Would you mind
talking with us for a bit?

03:36.210 --> 03:38.340
Of course, that's fine.

03:38.880 --> 03:39.720
Right?

03:39.720 --> 03:44.090
Yeah, we haven't partnered up
with anyone yet either.

03:44.090 --> 03:46.720
I'm glad you catch on quickly.

03:46.720 --> 03:51.350
To start, we'd like you to partner
with Sudo over here.

03:51.350 --> 03:55.110
In that case...
how about this much?

03:55.110 --> 03:57.820
What, you're asking for points?!

03:57.820 --> 04:00.110
And 50,000 is way too high!

04:00.110 --> 04:04.030
Senior, please don't joke around.

04:04.030 --> 04:07.120
Not 50,000, but 500,000.

04:07.120 --> 04:09.120
F-Five hundred thousand?!

04:09.120 --> 04:14.830
We've already been approached
by Class A and Class C.

04:14.830 --> 04:17.880
We have no intention of
selling ourselves cheaply.

04:17.880 --> 04:21.209
All right, we'll take that
into consideration.

04:21.209 --> 04:24.890
Also, we have another request.

04:24.890 --> 04:29.140
Could you introduce us to some
of your classmates in Class D?

04:29.140 --> 04:33.190
That's... a bit difficult.

04:33.190 --> 04:38.150
Yeah, if we act on our own,
Hosen will get mad at us.

04:38.150 --> 04:39.360
Right?

04:42.400 --> 04:45.780
Damn it, they're totally trying
to take advantage of us.

04:45.780 --> 04:50.160
They said Hosen would get angry
if they acted on their own, right?

04:50.160 --> 04:53.660
But if they do that, won't they end up
with no one left to pair with?

04:53.660 --> 04:57.670
It's only the second-years who fear
the penalty of not finding a partner.

04:57.670 --> 04:59.090
Hosen is thinking that

04:59.090 --> 05:02.670
he can use that to squeeze as many
Private Points out of us as possible.

05:02.670 --> 05:07.090
If we keep asking around blindly
like this, we'll get the same result.

05:07.970 --> 05:09.430
So what should we do?

05:10.180 --> 05:14.600
This time, I have no intention of
playing the money game.

05:15.190 --> 05:19.400
Even if we finish in first place overall,
we'll only gain 50 Class Points.

05:19.400 --> 05:24.440
Converted into Private Points,
that's just a little over two million.

05:24.440 --> 05:28.240
In other words,
if we pay 500,000 per person,

05:28.240 --> 05:30.950
we'd be in the red
after paying just five people.

05:30.950 --> 05:35.960
That's why I think we shouldn't
spend points recklessly here.

05:36.580 --> 05:41.960
For our next move, we should aim
to negotiate with Class 1-D.

05:41.960 --> 05:47.130
However, relying solely
on Hosen's class is too risky.

05:47.130 --> 05:52.060
To find capable partners, we'll have
no choice but to approach many people.

05:52.970 --> 05:54.470
Hey!

05:54.470 --> 05:59.190
If you're looking for a capable partner,
I'm right here, you know?

06:03.230 --> 06:05.740
Were you eavesdropping on us?

06:05.740 --> 06:07.740
Oh, gosh, no, Senior.

06:07.740 --> 06:11.370
I just shouted out because I only
happened to hear what you were saying.

06:11.370 --> 06:14.870
I'm Ichika Amasawa from Class 1-A.

06:14.870 --> 06:17.960
My academic ability score is A.

06:17.960 --> 06:20.000
Want to partner up?

06:20.000 --> 06:24.550
I appreciate the offer,
but instead of partnering with me,

06:24.550 --> 06:27.510
could you partner up with Sudo?

06:29.010 --> 06:32.260
Senior Sudo's academic score is E+, huh.

06:32.260 --> 06:35.770
Well, I'll lend you a hand.

06:35.770 --> 06:37.270
For real?!

06:37.890 --> 06:41.860
You know, I like strong guys.

06:42.480 --> 06:44.110
What are you talking about?

06:44.110 --> 06:49.490
I'm not talking about mental strength,
but physical strength.

06:49.490 --> 06:52.990
I'll gather strong guys
and have them fight it out,

06:52.990 --> 06:58.500
and whoever's the strongest
gets to be my partner.

06:58.500 --> 07:02.500
Are you joking?
There's no way we can agree to that.

07:02.500 --> 07:06.050
Why not? I'm serious.

07:06.050 --> 07:09.050
I like strong guys.

07:11.090 --> 07:13.220
Let's go, Suzune.

07:13.220 --> 07:15.560
She's just messing with us.

07:15.560 --> 07:17.060
Seems like it.

07:20.520 --> 07:24.650
All right, I'll give you another chance,
so forgive me.

07:25.640 --> 07:26.780
Another chance?

07:26.780 --> 07:33.030
Besides strong guys,
I also like guys who can cook.

07:33.820 --> 07:38.040
If you can make a dish I request and
it tastes good, I'll partner with you.

07:38.040 --> 07:40.620
C-Cooking?!

07:40.620 --> 07:43.830
But I've never cooked in my life!

07:43.830 --> 07:47.550
Would it be okay if
I cooked instead of Sudo?

07:47.550 --> 07:49.220
Nope.

07:49.220 --> 07:53.050
Didn't you hear me?
I said I like guys who can cook.

07:54.300 --> 07:55.800
Ayanokoji.

07:55.800 --> 08:00.560
I recall you once said you're
good at cooking, didn't you?

08:00.560 --> 08:05.810
Yeah. It wouldn't be an exaggeration
to say it's my only strong point.

08:05.810 --> 08:09.320
Then how about Ayanokoji instead?

08:09.320 --> 08:13.150
That's fine,
but is he really that good?

08:13.150 --> 08:15.570
My judgment will be pretty strict,
you know?

08:15.570 --> 08:17.870
That'll be fine.

08:17.870 --> 08:19.080
Right?

08:19.080 --> 08:21.080
Yeah, I guess.

08:21.080 --> 08:23.080
Then it's settled!

08:23.670 --> 08:27.460
If you can't serve me a delicious
homemade dish after school tomorrow,

08:27.460 --> 08:30.340
this deal is off!

08:30.340 --> 08:32.630
I'm counting on you, Ayanokoji!

08:32.630 --> 08:36.340
Use your cooking skills and
get me a partner!

08:37.600 --> 08:41.140
See you tomorrow, then!
Bye-bye!

08:42.600 --> 08:47.110
Horikita, you already know this.
My cooking skills are...

08:47.110 --> 08:50.980
Be quiet for now.
I'm thinking of a plan.

08:52.490 --> 08:54.990
As of this morning,
56 pairs have already been formed.

08:54.990 --> 08:59.990
So more than 30% of the students
have already secured partners.

09:00.790 --> 09:03.870
I guess it's about time
I started making serious moves.

09:04.710 --> 09:08.000
Good morning, Senior Ayanokoji.

09:08.000 --> 09:12.010
I apologize for Hosen's
rude behavior the other day.

09:12.010 --> 09:14.630
It's nothing you need to apologize for.

09:14.630 --> 09:19.680
No, I was with him to stop him
from acting like that,

09:19.680 --> 09:22.020
and it made me realize
how powerless I am.

09:22.680 --> 09:26.520
Sociable, polite,
and highly intelligent.

09:27.060 --> 09:29.360
Then why is she in Class D?

09:29.900 --> 09:31.780
And more importantly...

09:32.820 --> 09:34.610
That look in her eyes back then...

09:36.150 --> 09:38.410
Have you already found a partner?

09:38.410 --> 09:40.160
Me?

09:40.160 --> 09:44.290
No, not yet. I've received
several offers and haven't decided.

09:44.950 --> 09:49.080
If you're okay with it, how about
we in Class D cooperate...

09:49.080 --> 09:51.460
...and help each other find partners?

09:51.460 --> 09:54.760
Cooperate with each other?

09:54.760 --> 09:55.920
Yeah.

09:56.410 --> 09:58.840
I'd like to agree,

09:58.840 --> 10:00.930
but there's one problem...

10:00.930 --> 10:02.930
Is it Hosen?

10:02.930 --> 10:09.440
Yes. Many students have already started
following his instructions obediently.

10:09.440 --> 10:13.230
Are you in some kind
of special position?

10:13.230 --> 10:16.950
You didn't seem intimidated by him.

10:16.950 --> 10:20.450
I will never yield to violence.

10:22.330 --> 10:26.620
In any case, if Hosen is the one
deciding what your class does,

10:26.620 --> 10:29.210
this plan might be
difficult to carry out.

10:30.210 --> 10:33.460
Um, if you're okay with it,

10:33.460 --> 10:36.970
would you like me to try
to arrange a meeting?

10:37.630 --> 10:41.970
Are you sure that's alright?
I think Horikita would be pleased too.

10:41.970 --> 10:45.720
Is Senior Horikita your class leader?

10:45.720 --> 10:47.240
Yeah.

10:47.240 --> 10:49.980
I'll let her know.

10:49.980 --> 10:52.480
Can we exchange contact information?

10:52.480 --> 10:56.730
Yes. I look forward to working
with you, Senior Ayanokoji!

10:58.740 --> 11:02.620
That's quite a bold move for you.

11:02.620 --> 11:04.120
Was it uncalled for?

11:04.120 --> 11:07.250
No. I couldn't ask for more.

11:07.250 --> 11:12.580
But isn't Hosen aiming for the kind of
money game you want to avoid?

11:12.580 --> 11:14.290
That may be true.

11:14.290 --> 11:18.010
But is he really only after points?

11:18.010 --> 11:22.510
You mean his target is our Class D?

11:22.510 --> 11:27.560
Even so, we can expect Hosen
won't be easy to deal with.

11:27.560 --> 11:30.690
As a backup, I've been discussing
whether we can form...

11:30.690 --> 11:34.020
...a cooperative relationship with
some students from Class 1-B.

11:34.020 --> 11:35.770
Speaking of Class B,

11:35.770 --> 11:39.780
you mean Yagami, the one who went to the
same middle school as you and Kushida?

11:40.320 --> 11:44.200
Kushida partnered with
Yagami yesterday.

11:44.200 --> 11:48.700
We're having him negotiate
behind the scenes.

11:48.700 --> 11:51.290
I'd like you to lend a hand as well.

11:51.290 --> 11:53.630
You mean the matter
with Amasawa, right?

11:53.630 --> 11:54.540
Yes.

11:55.380 --> 11:57.250
The plan is already set.

12:02.220 --> 12:04.050
First, a cutting board,

12:04.050 --> 12:05.800
then a knife,

12:05.800 --> 12:09.060
and after that, a bowl
and a whisk, and also...

12:09.060 --> 12:10.770
Wait a second.

12:10.770 --> 12:13.310
I already have cooking tools in my room.

12:13.310 --> 12:17.570
It's fine, it's fine. I just want you
to buy these tools for me.

12:18.320 --> 12:20.820
And they're all high quality, too.

12:20.820 --> 12:24.570
Ah, a petty knife is a must as well.

12:24.570 --> 12:26.990
Just to confirm,
who's paying for all this?

12:26.990 --> 12:30.830
Oh, come on. Obviously you,
Senior Ayanokoji.

12:30.830 --> 12:32.750
I figured as much.

12:33.830 --> 12:38.090
Well, I guess I can think of it as getting
to use high-quality tools later.

12:38.090 --> 12:41.670
Oh, and like I said,
they're for me,

12:41.670 --> 12:43.590
so don't use them
for everyday cooking, okay?

12:43.970 --> 12:45.430
Are you some kind of demon?

12:47.100 --> 12:48.600
Excuse me!

12:50.010 --> 12:53.350
Oh wow, it's really tidy in here.

12:54.350 --> 12:57.400
While I'm cooking, just relax
and make yourself comfortable.

12:57.400 --> 12:58.860
Thanks, Senior.

12:58.860 --> 13:03.110
Oh, and looking things up on your phone
while cooking is cheating, okay?

13:03.110 --> 13:04.860
Wow, you're strict.

13:04.860 --> 13:06.860
So you're not feeling confident?

13:07.370 --> 13:09.330
That's not it.

13:09.330 --> 13:11.660
I'll leave my phone here.

13:11.660 --> 13:14.120
So, what am I making?

13:14.540 --> 13:16.580
All right, I'll tell you.

13:16.580 --> 13:19.630
What I'm going to have you cook is...

13:20.250 --> 13:22.130
Tom yum kung!

13:22.570 --> 13:24.510
Tom yum kung, huh...

13:25.760 --> 13:28.890
I'm counting on you, Senior.

13:29.720 --> 13:33.640
I heard everything. Can't believe
she asked for tom yum kung...

13:33.640 --> 13:36.350
I'll need you to guide me
through the steps.

13:36.350 --> 13:39.150
Use the knife the way
I taught you yesterday.

13:39.150 --> 13:44.030
Let's finish cooking
within 15 to 30 minutes.

13:44.030 --> 13:45.150
Understood?

13:45.150 --> 13:49.570
Now then, let's see
how well I can make this.

13:53.660 --> 13:57.670
Wow, amazing!
You're handling it really well.

13:59.330 --> 14:01.670
Okay, let's dig in.

14:04.670 --> 14:07.430
Oh, this is actually pretty good!

14:07.430 --> 14:10.140
Ah, an apple bunny!

14:13.850 --> 14:15.600
Thanks for the meal.

14:16.310 --> 14:19.100
So, Senior, your tom yum kung is...

14:21.310 --> 14:24.690
Yeah, I guess it's so-so.

14:26.610 --> 14:29.450
Anyway, let's clean up.

14:29.450 --> 14:30.660
I'll handle it.

14:30.660 --> 14:31.950
No, it's okay.

14:31.950 --> 14:35.240
I made you cook all this for me,
so let me at least do this much.

14:35.240 --> 14:36.950
Fine, then.

14:36.950 --> 14:40.460
By the way, what's my score?

14:40.460 --> 14:45.000
Honestly, I can't really say you passed,

14:45.000 --> 14:47.720
but since you bought all this
expensive stuff for me,

14:47.720 --> 14:52.470
I'll acknowledge your effort and agree
to partner with Senior Sudo.

14:52.470 --> 14:54.220
Thank you.

14:54.220 --> 14:55.720
It's fine, it's fine.

14:55.720 --> 14:58.730
You can thank me as much as you want.

14:58.730 --> 15:02.730
Well then, it'll get late if I stay,
so I'll head back now.

15:02.730 --> 15:03.900
Yeah.

15:03.900 --> 15:07.740
See you, Senior Ayanokoji.
Bye-bye.

15:10.490 --> 15:14.200
Good work. It seems things
worked out, somehow.

15:14.200 --> 15:16.990
Sudo's issue has been resolved.

15:16.990 --> 15:19.080
That was an excellent outcome.

15:19.080 --> 15:23.130
It feels like we were saved by Amasawa's
generous judgment, though.

15:23.130 --> 15:26.130
I'll let you know
once Nanase contacts me.

15:26.130 --> 15:26.880
Got it.

15:27.880 --> 15:30.880
If Amasawa really is
from the White Room,

15:30.880 --> 15:33.640
it wouldn't be strange for her
to have set something up.

15:34.350 --> 15:38.560
What matters is, she chose
to pair with Sudo instead of me.

15:38.560 --> 15:44.650
I suppose that rules out the possibility
of her being a White Room suspect.

15:45.650 --> 15:48.150
(Tsubasa Nanase)
(I'll see you after school tomorrow)

15:50.150 --> 15:52.660
(Tsubasa Nanase)
(I'll see you after school tomorrow)

15:53.660 --> 15:59.160
It seems the students we reached out to
have all received offers from Class C.

15:59.160 --> 16:04.170
And they're offering 10,000 points
if they turn down Class A's offer.

16:04.170 --> 16:06.170
Are they stupid or what?

16:06.920 --> 16:12.680
It seems Ryuen really intends
to throw down the gauntlet against me.

16:13.110 --> 16:14.680
So, what are you going to do?

16:14.680 --> 16:17.640
Tell the first-years this:

16:17.640 --> 16:21.430
We're prepared to match
whatever amount Ryuen offers.

16:22.100 --> 16:25.900
However, even if they accept,

16:25.910 --> 16:28.570
they are not to form
a partnership yet.

16:28.570 --> 16:30.690
Huh? What does that mean?

16:30.690 --> 16:33.200
I seriously don't get it.

16:34.490 --> 16:40.410
Ryuen, your strategy is actually
quite convenient for me.

16:40.410 --> 16:43.210
I have no idea what's going on...

16:43.210 --> 16:47.960
Isn't it fine?
If the princess says so.

16:47.960 --> 16:54.470
Ryuen's large-scale buyout strategy
itself isn't bad.

16:54.470 --> 16:55.510
However,

16:55.510 --> 17:00.970
continuing to compete with us over
the same students is clearly a mistake.

17:00.970 --> 17:04.390
But if he's making that many offers,

17:04.390 --> 17:07.730
doesn't that mean he's stockpiled
a ton of Private Points?

17:07.730 --> 17:10.690
Well, who knows?

17:10.690 --> 17:14.240
Making offers costs nothing,
and you can do it even without money.

17:14.240 --> 17:17.200
So he's just pretending to have money?

17:17.200 --> 17:20.790
What does Class C gain from that?

17:20.790 --> 17:26.079
If Ryuen weren't involved, we could
attract many top students

17:26.079 --> 17:28.500
with the brand power of Class A alone.

17:28.500 --> 17:35.510
But Class C has forced us into
a money game as well.

17:35.510 --> 17:38.010
And what comes next?

17:38.010 --> 17:43.770
They'll drive up the price and force us
to spend as many points as possible.

17:43.770 --> 17:47.270
I see...
So it's like poker.

17:47.270 --> 17:54.280
However, he underestimated
the reputation of Class A.

17:55.030 --> 17:58.160
It seems the Class B student
we tried to recruit for 200,000 points

17:58.160 --> 18:00.280
has put our offer on hold.

18:00.280 --> 18:03.540
Why? Is 200,000 not enough?

18:03.540 --> 18:05.040
Calm down.

18:05.040 --> 18:08.040
I know exactly what they're after.

18:08.040 --> 18:12.420
Tell them we'll pay 100,000 upfront
and 200,000 after the exam.

18:12.420 --> 18:14.050
Y-You're serious?

18:14.050 --> 18:18.050
Most of them won't make a decision.

18:18.050 --> 18:21.300
They'll be expecting Sakayanagi
to raise the offer.

18:21.300 --> 18:25.560
Isn't that basically self-destructive?

18:25.560 --> 18:29.810
Even if we had equal funds,
we'd lose in brand power.

18:29.810 --> 18:34.440
That "Class A brand"
is just for show right now.

18:34.440 --> 18:38.700
Even so, what do we do if the prices
keep rising like this?

18:38.700 --> 18:40.950
We don't have to pay.

18:40.950 --> 18:42.070
Huh?

18:42.070 --> 18:48.580
What I'm trying to figure out is what kind
of students this year's first-years are.

18:48.580 --> 18:53.090
Those who can be swayed by money
can always be brought to our side later.

18:53.090 --> 18:57.090
What matters are the others.

18:57.090 --> 19:02.600
I had no intention of gaining class points
that aren't even worth pocket change.

19:02.600 --> 19:05.350
If we're going to crush Class A,

19:05.350 --> 19:10.480
we need to wait for a moment when Class
Points fluctuate far more dramatically.

19:12.520 --> 19:13.360
Oh?

19:13.850 --> 19:16.110
What an unusual guest.

19:16.110 --> 19:18.570
Hello, Shiina.

19:18.570 --> 19:23.240
We're going to have a discussion,
so it might get a bit noisy today.

19:23.240 --> 19:28.120
I see. In that case, the seats
in the back would be best.

19:28.120 --> 19:29.870
Thank you.

19:29.870 --> 19:32.380
Are things coming
along okay in Class C?

19:32.380 --> 19:36.000
Yes. It seems there's
a lot going on right now.

19:37.760 --> 19:42.300
Putting Nanase aside,
the real question is how Hosen will act.

19:42.300 --> 19:43.640
Yeah.

19:43.640 --> 19:47.720
Things could change a lot depending on
whether he shows up or not.

19:47.720 --> 19:50.430
Sorry to have kept you waiting, Senior.

19:51.230 --> 19:54.150
Let me introduce myself one more time.
my name is Suzune Horikita.

19:54.150 --> 19:56.480
Thank you for taking the time
to speak with us today.

19:56.480 --> 19:58.980
I'm... um, I mean...

19:58.980 --> 20:02.030
My name is Tsubasa Nanase.

20:02.030 --> 20:05.740
I should be the one thanking you.

20:05.740 --> 20:07.460
Let me get straight to the point.

20:07.460 --> 20:09.700
What I want to discuss today is

20:09.700 --> 20:12.500
different from forming
a partnership based on points.

20:12.910 --> 20:14.380
Yes, I understand.

20:14.380 --> 20:16.380
You're proposing
a cooperative relationship

20:16.380 --> 20:18.300
where we cover for
each other's students...

20:18.300 --> 20:19.960
...who are academically weaker, correct?

20:19.960 --> 20:23.430
Yes. Since you came here
already understanding that,

20:23.430 --> 20:25.760
does that mean there's
room for negotiation?

20:25.760 --> 20:28.930
I'd like to think so...

20:28.930 --> 20:34.020
Hosen's approach is one of
extreme individualism.

20:34.510 --> 20:35.810
If things continue like this,

20:35.810 --> 20:39.230
students with low academic ability
won't be able to find partners...

20:39.230 --> 20:41.030
...and will be left behind.

20:41.030 --> 20:46.740
But what I truly fear is that
this individualism will persist,

20:46.740 --> 20:49.790
and the class will lose
its unity going forward.

20:49.790 --> 20:51.160
I see.

20:51.160 --> 20:52.960
If individualism continues to intensify,

20:52.960 --> 20:56.020
the class won't be able
to function as one...

20:56.030 --> 20:58.280
...when facing future exams
that require teamwork.

20:58.280 --> 20:59.300
Exactly.

20:59.300 --> 21:04.550
That's why I came to negotiate
on my own, for the sake of the class.

21:06.410 --> 21:09.720
Then let me ask a more direct question.

21:09.720 --> 21:11.640
Approximately how many students

21:11.640 --> 21:15.770
in Class 1-D are currently
struggling to find partners?

21:15.770 --> 21:18.810
At the moment, there are
close to 15 students.

21:19.270 --> 21:21.310
That's more than I expected.

21:22.030 --> 21:24.860
Nanase, if you're willing,
I'd like to propose

21:24.860 --> 21:27.450
a major arrangement between our classes.

21:27.450 --> 21:30.450
A major arrangement?

21:30.450 --> 21:35.870
I'm thinking that you and I
could decide on 15 partnerships...

21:35.870 --> 21:39.210
...and finalize them all at once.

21:43.130 --> 21:46.340
I think it's a wonderful proposal, but...

21:46.340 --> 21:50.890
Hosen would never approve
of helping you for free.

21:50.890 --> 21:54.640
Why not? There shouldn't be any
disadvantage for him.

21:54.640 --> 21:57.220
Even so...

21:57.230 --> 21:59.650
I still don't think Hosen would approve.

21:59.650 --> 22:02.400
I see.
So that's how it is.

22:04.150 --> 22:09.110
There's one thing I've come to understand
about Hosen's way of thinking.

22:27.170 --> 22:33.810
Ah, eyes filled with a cold, dark light

22:33.810 --> 22:38.390
Lips that have swallowed all flavors,
yet remain empty

22:38.390 --> 22:42.720
"What could you be thinking?"

22:42.720 --> 22:47.160
It's so dim I can't see it

22:47.170 --> 22:52.950
The veil of a liar cannot be torn away

22:52.950 --> 22:58.580
Janus gazes at the room
where butterflies dance

22:58.580 --> 23:03.100
It's survival of the fittest out here

23:03.100 --> 23:08.130
One might already be gone by tomorrow

23:08.130 --> 23:13.300
I want to be buried,
I'm sure that's what I want

23:13.300 --> 23:18.440
With a knife of either
adoration or hatred, ah

23:18.440 --> 23:23.410
Not denying everything in this world

23:23.410 --> 23:30.190
Poison is medicine,
for the monster that devours everything

23:33.910 --> 23:36.950
I want to know what you really are
